d `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n-- [ ] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n-- [ ] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n+- [x] T006 [P] In `CA`, add `export interface CommandRow { readonly command: string; readonly policy?: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string }`, an empty marked block `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` holding `export const COMMAND_ROWS: Readonly<Record<string, CommandRow>> = {};` and `export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {};` then `// END GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, and `export function commandRowFor(id: string): CommandRow | undefined` that reads `COMMAND_ROWS` with `Object.hasOwn`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"GENERATED COMMAND ROWS\" $CA` prints 2.\n+- [x] T007 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`SCH`), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n+- [x] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n+- [x] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n+- [x] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n \n ### Wave 2\n-- [ ] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n+- [x] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 3\n-- [ ] T016 In `publicRecommendation` (`H`), add `