e `use` head and both sides of the `ambiguous` head. Every part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`. Rewrite `doctorCommandString` to return `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id. Leave the `Also:` line's trigger unchanged. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" $R` prints nothing.\n+- [x] T018 In `CLI`, pass the prompt to `degradedRecommendations` and export it. For an entry with a `commandRowFor(entry.skill)` row: when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command (the text before the first space), emit `skillId`, `kind: 'command'`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. Otherwise emit the row's `ownerSkillId` as `skillId` with `kind: 'skill'`, and drop it when that skill is already in the list. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 4\n-- [ ] T019 In `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`H`), build `alreadyOffered` from the `command` fields of the recommendations and delete `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID`. When a hub gets an attached command, also set `policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` when that key exists. Verify: after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"options\":{\"includeCompiledRoute\":true}}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {skillId,command,policy}'` prints `{\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}`, and `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T020 Delete `renderDoctorCommandStrings` and the `R` entry from `generatedSources` in `D`, then delete the `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block from `R`, then run `node $D`. Verify: `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS|renderDoctorCommandStrings\" $D $R` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh` and `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T019 In `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`H`), build `alreadyOffered` from the `command` fields of the recommendations and delete `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID`. When a hub gets an attached command, also set `policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` when that key exists. Verify: after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"options\":{\"includeCompiledRoute\":true}}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {skillId,command,policy}'` prints `{\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}`, and `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T020 Delete `renderDoctorCommandStrings` and the `R` entry from `generatedSources` in `D`, then delete the `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block from `R`, then run `node $D`. Verify: `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS|renderDoctorCommandStrings\" $D $R` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh` and `$TC` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 5\n - [ ] T021 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. It renders six constructed results through `renderAdvisorBrief` and asserts the six heads in `plan.md` section 3 exactly, that each head before `\\nDirectives:` is at most 320 characters and that no head contains `command-`. Add one row each for a missing field filled from `COMMAND_ROWS`, an id with no row and a missing policy. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md b/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\nindex 7a58cad562..03b2722dbc 100644\n--- a/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\n+++ b/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\n@@ -77,27 +77,27 @@ Worker waves. Tasks in 